# Round r8host, the landing A/B: the V4.1 host tier's routed gates and ups read from the r8 sidecar
# through the row-lane tile (qdot::dot_q3k_r8_cols) against the source's rows (dot_row_cols), one
# binary, BLOOMERY_R8=on (the default) against =off; both write the same bits. The union's kernel an
# expert of m columns is a + c m us: today 30.2 + 22.2 m (measured), r8 38 + 13.05 m [derived,
# h3tile-b section 7; 59.4 + 14.63 m as measured under the bench queue, rig-log 09-25#h3tile-ab, the
# band's low edge]. Flow model (tools/flow, main cbc712a, today's flow B1+T+G, hot list 384): the union
# a layer-batch lcg 62.6 -> 46.4 [44.6-51.9] ms at P = 512 and 63.3 -> 46.9 [45.1-52.4] at 4096, prose
# 36.4 -> 26.6 [24.4-29.7] and 37.7 -> 27.4 [25.2-30.6]; pp lcg 152.4 -> 188.8 and 266.2 -> 347.9,
# prose 221.5 -> 267.0 and 400.4 -> 432.2 [derived]; each effect band is the on/off ratio under the
# same constant moves. Without the hot list (the README's lcg condition) the lcg bands are
# +15.8..+28.9 (P = 512) and +19.7..+37.3 (P = 4096). The weakest row is prose P = 4096: its source
# value 400.4 is the model's after G, never measured (cardtile-ab read 292 before G), and r8 moves its
# wall onto the card; read it as a screen. Decode moves 0: a host token-layer reads ~4.7 experts'
# gate/up, 47.8 MB, 359 us at 133 GB/s, against 169 (today) and 89 us (r8) of compute [derived].
kind: ab
question: does reading the host tier's gates and ups from the r8 sidecar shorten the V4.1 prompt
  call by the union's per-column term, as the flow model's host-bound wall says?
term: pp tok/s @ P = 512, lcg prompt, hot list 384, A6000, plan (a), CED on - (on - off) / off,
  paired by round
unit: %
predict: +14.8..+27.0
rounds: 2
sd: 1.1 % rig-log 09-25#v41-prefill-s14, two binaries' per-round pp ratios, one run's SD about 0.55
  and 1.1 %; the larger
condition: the r8host binary, both arms in one lease through its lever, the four r8 arms before the
  four source arms so the one-slot rotation switches the page cache between the two files twice a
  round: BLOOMERY_AB_ROUNDS=2 BLOOMERY_BOX_ENV='BLOOMERY_HOT_LIST=/root/bloomery-data/router/hotlist-384.txt
  BLOOMERY_STEP_STATS=1 BLOOMERY_LEASE_CARD=docs/cards/r8host-pp.card' just depth-gpu-ds41 512 4096
  prose:512 prose:4096 512@BLOOMERY_R8=off 4096@BLOOMERY_R8=off prose:512@BLOOMERY_R8=off
  prose:4096@BLOOMERY_R8=off. A switch reads the other file's host gates and ups, 12,692 experts x
  10,137,600 B = 128.7 GB, inside the arm's load, before its timed window: ~19 s [derived: 128.7 GB at the
  6.83 GB/s r8land's chunked host-set walk read from the NVMe, 190.63 GB in 27.9-28.1 s on plan (b),
  runtime values; the one-thread sidecar populate it replaced read 1.35-1.43 GB/s];
  host_populate prints the sidecar's bytes. The two files' gates and ups do not fit the page cache
  together, so the populate can lose pages before the window: an r8 row's decode steps (the stat step
  lines BLOOMERY_STEP_STATS prints) must fault no more (majflt) than the same prompt's source row -
  the engram rows, outside the host set, fault alike in both - and a row past that, [cpu-busy] or
  [other-busy] is void; if the first arm after a switch shows the excess, re-sit with
  BLOOMERY_HOST_LOCK=1. The other rows are read against their own bands by the same decisions: lcg P = 4096
  +18.6..+35.0, prose P = 512 +14.6..+23.4, prose P = 4096 +4.1..+11.1 (inside the ruler at two
  rounds, h 4.7 %: a screen; three resolve it, h 2.5 %). The arms' decode rows, tg96 at depth 512 and
  4096, predict 0 and are a screen. Box time ~32-33 min [derived: 16 runs of ~117 s, the cardtile
  lease's, plus four switches of ~19 s], past 30 min, so the sitting needs the user's approval; P = 512 alone
  (four arms) is ~18 min
decide-in: keep r8 on as the default; write stat prefill split's union into a_r8 and c_r8 of
  tools/flow/constants.tsv as measured values in place of the derived ones
decide-below: read union per layer-batch in stat prefill split: near the off arm's, the lanes did
  not take the tile's column share (the per-group cost table, the 18-group steal block) - time the
  engine's r8 lane beside the bench's unionr8 arm (just time-cpu-v41-host, its own card) before the
  next host round
decide-above: the union fell under the card route: re-derive the wall with the card as the bound
  and move host streaming (the hottest host experts on the card) ahead of the next host-side lever
